  "id": "COMPOUND:15568 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate and SNU1 through a series of molecular interactions. Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate is identified as a target for multiple enzymes, including CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is in turn targeted by 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and Basiliskamide B. These compounds ultimately target SNU1, indicating a possible pathway involving sialyltransferase activity and subsequent signaling. Additionally, Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate is also linked to Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is targeted by Oleamide, another compound that ultimately affects SNU1. While the exact mechanism linking Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate to SNU1 remains unclear, the evidence suggests a network of interactions involving enzyme inhibition and signaling pathways that may contribute to the observed effects. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with multiple layers of molecular interactions potentially influencing SNU1.",
